        studies: [{year:2022, finding:"Preserved muscle mass in elderly & during bedrest/calorie restriction (meta)", source:"J Cachexia Sarcopenia Muscle"}, {year:2023, finding:"Enhanced strength & lean mass with resistance training", source:"J Strength Cond Res"}, {year:2024, finding:"Reduced muscle loss post-surgery/illness (RCTs)", source:"Clin Nutr"}],
        dosage: "3 g daily (split 1g 3x or 3g pre/post workout)", synergies: ["creatine", "eaa", "protein", "vitamin d"],
        gorkipedia: "Gorkipedia Entry: HMB is the anti-catabolic insurance policy. Especially valuable for older adults (sarcopenia prevention), dieters, or anyone in a catabolic state (illness, travel, high stress). 3g is the studied dose. Free acid form (HMB-FA) may be slightly better absorbed than calcium HMB. Stack with creatine for synergy.",
