        dosage: "Common mistaken: 400–800 IU daily 'for heart/anti-aging'", synergies: [],
        gorkipedia: "Gorkipedia Entry (WARNING): The famous 'antioxidant' that turned out to raise death rates when supplemented high-dose. Food sources (nuts, seeds, oils) are fine. Isolated high-dose dl-alpha-tocopherol is the problematic form in most studies. Do not exceed 100-200 IU supplemental unless specific medical reason and monitored.",
