        gorkipedia: "Gorkipedia Entry (WARNING): DHEA is a real hormone, not a vitamin. Selling it OTC was a regulatory loophole. Self-experimenting with it without frequent bloodwork (total T, free T, E2, DHT, PSA, liver, lipids) is playing Russian roulette with your endocrine system. Most men over 40 who 'feel low T' have lifestyle issues, not DHEA deficiency. Get proper TRT evaluation instead of guessing.",
