        studies: [{year:2005, finding:"High doses can suppress endogenous secretion and alter reproductive hormones", source:"J Clin Endocrinol Metab"}, {year:2012, finding:"No additional sleep benefit above 1-3mg in most meta-analyses; side effects increase", source:"Sleep Med Rev"}, {year:2022, finding:"Chronic high-dose users show blunted natural melatonin rhythms", source:"J Pineal Res"}],
        dosage: "Common mistaken: 5–30 mg nightly 'for deep sleep and longevity/anti-cancer'", synergies: [],
        gorkipedia: "Gorkipedia Entry (WARNING): We added low-dose melatonin as beneficial. High-dose chronic use is the opposite. Your pineal gland stops making its own when you hammer it with 10-20mg every night. Many people who 'can't sleep without 10mg melatonin' created the dependency themselves. Taper down to 0.3-1mg or use behavioral methods instead.",
